        sloka: "utkrāmantaṁ sthitaṁ vāpi bhuñjānaṁ vā guṇānvitam\nvimūḍhā nānupaśhyanti paśhyanti jñāna-chakṣhuṣhaḥ",
        meaning: "The ignorant do not perceive the soul as it resides in the body, and as it enjoys sense objects; nor do they perceive it when it departs.  But those who possess the eyes of knowledge can behold it.",
